# Lanes append requirements to the same spec files in parallel; a union
# merge keeps both sides. `openspec validate --all --strict` runs in every
# round's checks and rejects a broken or duplicated requirement, so a bad
# union cannot land unnoticed. READMEs and findings.md are left out on
# purpose: their lines are edited in place, where a union would keep both
# the old and the new line.
openspec/specs/*/spec.md merge=union
